    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Luis Arraez** (67.31) and **Taylor Ward** (67.28), who present the most compelling profiles. **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a plus-park environment and a favorable matchup against the hittable Griffin Canning, with his leadoff positioning providing a 10% boost to his efficiency score. Similarly, **Matt Chapman** (66.77) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.52) are high-floor staples; while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** faces a tougher test in Jack Flaherty, his elite baseline projection keeps him as a mandatory start. We are also capitalizing on the high park factor for **Gavin Sheets** (64.98), whose combination of power potential and a favorable spot in the order makes him a strong play despite the presence of Shane Baz.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Gleyber Torres** (49.70) on the bench. While his order position suggested upside, he fell just short of displacing **Drew Gilbert** (50.80) because the optimizer heavily favored the latter\u2019s dynamic platoon advantage against Javier Assad. **Jonathan Aranda** (55.26) also sits on the fringe of the starting rotation; though his overall score is respectable, his sub-par platoon split against a southpaw like Sam Aldegheri suppresses his ceiling. We are currently monitoring all lineups as \"Pending,\" and should **Jonathan Aranda** shift down the order or be platooned out, we have the flexibility to pull from our bench depth. Investors should note that while **Daulton Varsho** (45.65) was considered for his stolen base potential, the low score against a competent arm like Ryan Weathers kept him sidelined to prioritize our daily game caps.",
